/*!
\page page_stmtdheader StMtdHeader

\brief Event-level header data for the STAR Muon Telescope Detector (MTD).

\section mtdheader_overview Overview

StMtdHeader stores per-event header data for the STAR Muon Telescope Detector (MTD),
fully operational since Run 12 (2012).

Like \ref StBTofHeader, it records per-fiber DAQ header and trigger words.
In addition it provides:
- \c mShouldHaveRejectEvent: a flag indicating whether the event would have been vetoed
  by the MTD di-muon trigger filter (−1=unknown, 0=not di-muon triggered, 1=should have been
  rejected, 2=passes filter cuts). Used in di-muon physics analyses.
- \c mTpcSectorMask: bitmask of TPC sectors used in the first-pass tracking iteration
  for MTD-matched muon candidates.

The object is held by \ref StMtdCollection via StEvent::mtdCollection()->mtdHeader().

\section mtdheader_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
TObject → StObject → StMtdHeader
\endcode

\section mtdheader_members Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| mFiberHeader[2] | Short_t | DAQ header words per fiber (default −1) |
| mFiberTriggerWord[2] | UInt_t | Trigger words per fiber |
| mTriggerTime[2] | UInt_t | Trigger time TDC counts per fiber |
| mShouldHaveRejectEvent | Int_t | Di-muon event filter status (−1/0/1/2) |
| mTpcSectorMask | UInt_t | TPC sector bitmask for first-pass tracking |

mShouldHaveRejectEvent values:
- −1: unknown / uninitialised
-  0: event was not triggered as di-muon
-  1: event should have been rejected by the di-muon filter
-  2: event passes di-muon filter cuts

\section mtdheader_methods Key Methods

- fiberHeader(fiberId) — DAQ header word for given fiber
- fiberTriggerWord(fiberId) — trigger word for given fiber
- triggerTime(fiberId) — trigger time TDC count for given fiber
- shouldHaveRejectEvent() — di-muon event filter status
- tpcSectorMask() — TPC sector bitmask

\section mtdheader_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StMtdCollection* coll = event->mtdCollection();
if (coll) {
    StMtdHeader* hdr = coll->mtdHeader();
    if (hdr) {
        unsigned int tTrig0 = hdr->triggerTime(0);
        unsigned int tTrig1 = hdr->triggerTime(1);
        int diMuonStatus    = hdr->shouldHaveRejectEvent();
        // 2 = passes di-muon filter; use for J/psi or Upsilon analyses
        unsigned int tpcMask = hdr->tpcSectorMask();
    }
}
\endcode

\see StMtdHit, StMtdRawHit, StMtdCollection
*/
